# Quote: Mario Bunge - Treatise on Basic Philosophy - Epistemology & Methodology III - Part II

> As for the epistemology of the doctrine, it is typically aprioristic and dogmatic: psychoanalysts have advanced the most outrageous conjectures as irrefutable theses, not as hypotheses to be tested. They possess the truth, so they need not search for it, and accordingly they have no use for the scientific ethos.

